# CarvePress Dogfood Site

The CarvePress documentation is now a CarvePress site. The pages under `docs/` are `.crv` source, the build writes `.site`, and GitHub Pages serves the result.

This matters because documentation examples are no longer decorative. The site uses home layout data, navigation, sidebars, generated blog pages, search, feed output, sitemap output, `llms.txt`, Shiki, compare blocks, playground blocks, includes, and link validation.

See [Getting Started](/guide/getting-started) for the shortest path to a new site.

